Package: flexPaths
Title: Causal Path-Specific Effect Estimation in Flexible Settings
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Xiaxian", "Ou", email = "xiaxian.ou@emory.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2905-8287")),
    person("Xinwei", "He", role = "aut",
           comment = "Contributed to the theoretical methodology"),
    person("Razieh", "Nabi", role = "aut",
           comment = "Contributed to the theoretical methodology")
    )
Description: Estimates causal path-specific means and effects with a single
    binary treatment or repeated binary treatments and multiple ordered
    mediators using wide-format data with one row per individual. Provides
    inverse probability weighting, plug-in g-computation,
    and influence-function-based estimators, with flexible models for
    treatment and outcome regressions. Supports linear and generalized linear
    models, Bayesian additive regression trees, and
    ensemble learning through 'SuperLearner'. Users can implement custom model
    fitting and prediction functions using the provided template. Methods for
    longitudinal settings are described in Ou, He and Nabi (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2610.34349>.
